.TH CF-AUTH 1 "September 2026" "cf-cli v1.1.2" "Cloudflare CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
cf-auth.1 \- Authentication methods, API tokens, and profiles for cf
.PP
\fBcf\fR provides flexible authentication suited for both interactive development and headless CI/CD pipelines.
.PP
.PP
.SH 1. AUTHENTICATION METHODS
.PP
.SS "Method A: API Token (Recommended)"
Cloudflare API tokens provide scoped, fine-grained access with configurable expiration dates.
.PP
Set the token via environment variable:
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
export CF_API_TOKEN="your-cloudflare-api-token"
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
\fI(Note: \fBCLOUDFLARE\fIAPI\fRTOKEN\fR is also supported as an alias)\fR.
.PP
.SS "Method B: Global API Key & Account Email (Legacy)"
If you require legacy authentication using your Cloudflare account email and Global API Key:
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
export CF_API_KEY="your-global-api-key"
export CF_API_EMAIL="you@example.com"
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.RS 2
\fBSecurity Warning:\fR Global API keys grant full administrative privileges across all zones and accounts. Creating an API Token with least-privilege permissions is strongly recommended.
.RE
.PP
.PP
.SH 2. CONFIG PROFILES (PERSISTENT CREDENTIALS)
.PP
\fBcf\fR allows storing multiple named authentication profiles in \fB~/.cf/config.json\fR. This makes switching between multiple accounts, clients, or environments seamless.
.PP
.SS "Creating Profiles"
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# Add a default profile with an API Token
cf config set --name default --token "cfut_..."

# Add a staging profile with an explicit account ID
cf config set --name staging --token "staging-token" --account-id "023e105f4ecef8ad9ca31a8372d0c353"

# Add a legacy key profile
cf config set --name legacy --key "global-key" --email "admin@example.com"
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.SS "Listing Profiles"
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf config list
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
Example Output:
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
┌──────────────────────┬──────────┬────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┬─────────┐
│ Profile              │ Auth     │ Email                          │ Account ID                         │ Default │
├──────────────────────┼──────────┼────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼─────────┤
│ default              │ token    │ -                              │ -                                  │ Yes     │
│ staging              │ token    │ -                              │ 023e105f4ecef8ad9ca31a8372d0c353   │         │
│ legacy               │ key      │ admin@example.com              │ -                                  │         │
└──────────────────────┴──────────┴────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┴─────────┘
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.SS "Switching Default Profile"
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf config use --name staging
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.SS "Using Profiles on a Per-Command Basis"
Override the active profile for a single invocation:
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
cf zones list --profile staging
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
.PP
.SH 3. RESOLUTION PRECEDENCE
.PP
When running any command, \fBcf\fR resolves credentials in this strict order:
.PP
.IP 1. 3
\fB--profile <name>\fR CLI flag
.IP 2. 3
\fBCF_PROFILE\fR environment variable
.IP 3. 3
\fBCF\fIAPI\fRTOKEN\fR (or \fBCLOUDFLARE\fIAPI\fRTOKEN\fR) environment variable
.IP 4. 3
\fBCF\fIAPI\fRKEY\fR + \fBCF\fIAPI\fREMAIL\fR environment variables
.IP 5. 3
\fBdefault\fR profile from \fB~/.cf/config.json\fR
.IP 6. 3
If none are found, the command exits with an authentication error
.PP
.PP
.SH 4. VERIFYING CREDENTIALS
.PP
To verify your credentials and check token validity:
.PP
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
# Verify current API token status
cf user tokens verify

# Inspect current user identity
cf user get
.ft
.fi
.PP
.PP
